[directions] d-17 [open] Quantify BBN + X-ray combined viable (m_s, sin^2 2theta) reg; d-18 [open] Survey 2024-2026 arXiv literature on sterile-neutrino DM pro; d-19 [open] Assess non-minimal production mechanisms and structure-forma; d-20 [open] Validate tool baselines and DW relic-density normalization a
**Plan** — 4 lines of investigation:
1. Quantify BBN + X-ray combined viable (m_s, sin^2 2theta) regions with sterile-nu tools — Directly answers which parameter space survives Yp/D/H/N_eff and radiative decay limits; provides tool-backed numbers for Yp, D/H, Delta N_eff, Gamma, E=m_s/2, flux vs limits
2. Survey 2024-2026 arXiv literature on sterile-neutrino DM production and X-ray searches — Grounds viability claims in published results; extracts verbatim limits for DW exclusion, XRISM 3.75 Ms stacking, and non-minimal production reopening parameter space
3. Assess non-minimal production mechanisms and structure-formation bounds against BBN/X-ray viability — Tests whether Shi-Fuller resonant (L~0.1-1), inflaton-decay (BR~1e-4), nuSMEFT freeze-in, and time-dependent mass models survive BBN Delta N_eff and X-ray limits while satisfying Lyman-alpha m_th bounds
4. Validate tool baselines and DW relic-density normalization against observations and literature — Prevents unverifiable Yp/D/H/N_eff and Omega_s h^2 claims; quantifies server vs published DW discrepancy that propagates to X-ray vs structure-formation tension (added by the critic)
Critic's view: revise — predict_sterile_nu_grid + scan_sterile_nu_parameters duplicates exclusion generation and risks >400 point limit. Specify grid size (e.g., 20x20=400) and use one scan method. Grid range 1e-3 to 1e2 keV x 1e-13 to 1e-1 must be checked against describe_sterile_nu_tools validity range first.; Claims to map SF/inflaton/freeze-in viable window m_s~5-20 keV, sin^2 2theta~1e-13 to 1e-10 with DW-mode tools. Tools do not compute non-minimal Omega_s h^2=0.12 contours; those regions can only be literature-quoted, not tool-validated. Must separate tool-backed DW/X-ray from literature-only non-minimal.; BBN-allowed definition inconsistent: brief uses Delta N_eff<0.3 and Yp/D/H within 2 sigma (Yp 0.245+/-0.003, D/H 2.53+/-0.03), success criteria uses Delta N_eff<0.548. Choose one bound and justify vs Planck 0.32-0.61 range..
